abstract: >-
  Rigorous interval-arithmetic certificate for the first 75,000 decimal
  digits of the Golomb-Dickman constant
  lambda = integral_0^infinity exp(-u - E_1(u)) du. The certificate gives
  integers Lambda_- < Lambda_+ and a scale S = 249341 such that lambda lies
  in [Lambda_-/2^S, Lambda_+/2^S] and
  floor(10^75000 Lambda_-/2^S) = floor(10^75000 Lambda_+/2^S); the digits
  are therefore proved by truncation. The interval width is
  5.8205594787 x 10^-75043, leaving about 42.235 guard digits. The package
  also contains the producing code and 4,767 checkpoints. A full Arb
  re-audit of all 476,648 nodes was not run; 2,000 nodes were checked.
  Earlier 50,000- and 40,000-digit certificates are kept in the repository.
